MathCAT (braille, Nemeth and UEB): linear UnicodeMath syntax characters

MateX keeps what is typed and not complete yet as linear text inside the
built equation, each build-up operator escaped (`x\_`, `x\▒`): the
converter gives it as `<mo intent=":text">`. Braille showed some of them
wrongly:

1. Nemeth `_` was empty, so `x_` (a subscript not typed yet) read as
   `x`. Nemeth has no underscore; an underscore denoting omission is the
   long dash (Nemeth Code 2022, 11.1.2), so a linear `_` (intent
   ":text") is `⠤⠤⠤⠤`. Every other `_` is still empty.
2. UnicodeMath's own syntax characters (▒ ┬ ┴ 〖 〗 ¦ ├ ┤ ▁ █ ⍁ ╱ ╲ ╳ ▢
   ☁ ✎ ⟌ ⟡ ⬄ ⇳ ⬆ ⬇ ⬌ ⬍ ⏜ ⏝ ⏠ ⏡) were not in either table and came out as
   a hex code of a dozen cells. Each is now its control word, as typed:
   backslash `⠸⠡` and the word's letters (▒ is `\of`). UEB's own `¦` (broken
   bar) is kept.

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on top of upstream 85c89a37. Only useful
upstream for UnicodeMath-aware callers; the Nemeth `_` rule may be worth
proposing to daisy/MathCAT.

diff --git a/Rules/Braille/Nemeth/unicode.yaml b/Rules/Braille/Nemeth/unicode.yaml
index 6ac9c74d..f7a57db5 100644
--- a/Rules/Braille/Nemeth/unicode.yaml
+++ b/Rules/Braille/Nemeth/unicode.yaml
@@ -260,7 +260,13 @@
  - "\\": [t: "⠸⠡"]              # 0x005C (Reverse solidus)
  - "]": [t: "⠈⠾"]               # 0x005D (Right square bracket)
  - "^": [t: "⠸⠣"]               # 0x005E (Circumflex accent)
- - "_": [t: ""]                 # 0x005F (Low line)
+ - "_":                         # 0x005F (Low line)
+     - test:
+        # MateX: an underscore left as linear text (a subscript not typed yet) marks an
+        # omission; Nemeth 2022, 11.1.2: an underscore denoting omission is the long dash.
+        if: "@intent=':text'"
+        then: [t: "⠤⠤⠤⠤"]
+        else: [t: ""]
  - "{": [t: "⠨⠷"]               # 0x007B (Left curly bracket)
  - "|":                # 0x007C (Vertical line)
      - test:
@@ -268,6 +274,37 @@
         then: [t: "w⠳w"]        # comparison (e.g., such that -- rule 145)
         else: [t: "⠳"]          # absolute value, others???
  - "}": [t: "⠨⠾"]               # 0x007D (Right curly bracket)
+ # MateX: UnicodeMath's own syntax characters, seen only while left as linear text
+ # (MateX's linear runs): their control words, as typed, not a hex code.
+ - "¦": [t: "⠸⠡⠁⠞⠕⠏"]         # 0x00A6 (\atop)
+ - "▒": [t: "⠸⠡⠕⠋"]             # 0x2592 (\of)
+ - "┬": [t: "⠸⠡⠃⠑⠇⠕⠺"]       # 0x252C (\below)
+ - "┴": [t: "⠸⠡⠁⠃⠕⠧⠑"]       # 0x2534 (\above)
+ - "〖": [t: "⠸⠡⠃⠑⠛⠊⠝"]       # 0x3016 (\begin)
+ - "〗": [t: "⠸⠡⠑⠝⠙"]           # 0x3017 (\end)
+ - "├": [t: "⠸⠡⠇⠑⠋⠞"]               # 0x251C (\left)
+ - "┤": [t: "⠸⠡⠗⠊⠛⠓⠞"]              # 0x2524 (\right)
+ - "▁": [t: "⠸⠡⠥⠝⠙⠑⠗⠃⠁⠗"]           # 0x2581 (\underbar)
+ - "█": [t: "⠸⠡⠑⠟⠁⠗⠗⠁⠽"]            # 0x2588 (\eqarray)
+ - "⍁": [t: "⠸⠡⠋⠗⠁⠉"]               # 0x2341 (\frac)
+ - "╱": [t: "⠸⠡⠉⠁⠝⠉⠑⠇"]             # 0x2571 (\cancel)
+ - "╲": [t: "⠸⠡⠃⠉⠁⠝⠉⠑⠇"]            # 0x2572 (\bcancel)
+ - "╳": [t: "⠸⠡⠭⠉⠁⠝⠉⠑⠇"]            # 0x2573 (\xcancel)
+ - "▢": [t: "⠸⠡⠗⠗⠑⠉⠞"]              # 0x25A2 (\rrect)
+ - "☁": [t: "⠸⠡⠃⠁⠉⠅⠉⠕⠇⠕⠗"]          # 0x2601 (\backcolor)
+ - "✎": [t: "⠸⠡⠉⠕⠇⠕⠗"]              # 0x270E (\color)
+ - "⟌": [t: "⠸⠡⠇⠕⠝⠛⠙⠊⠧"]            # 0x27CC (\longdiv)
+ - "⟡": [t: "⠸⠡⠏⠓⠁⠝⠞⠕⠍"]            # 0x27E1 (\phantom)
+ - "⬄": [t: "⠸⠡⠓⠏⠓⠁⠝⠞⠕⠍"]           # 0x2B04 (\hphantom)
+ - "⇳": [t: "⠸⠡⠧⠏⠓⠁⠝⠞⠕⠍"]           # 0x21F3 (\vphantom)
+ - "⬆": [t: "⠸⠡⠁⠎⠍⠁⠎⠓"]             # 0x2B06 (\asmash)
+ - "⬇": [t: "⠸⠡⠙⠎⠍⠁⠎⠓"]             # 0x2B07 (\dsmash)
+ - "⬌": [t: "⠸⠡⠓⠎⠍⠁⠎⠓"]             # 0x2B0C (\hsmash)
+ - "⬍": [t: "⠸⠡⠎⠍⠁⠎⠓"]              # 0x2B0D (\smash)
+ - "⏜": [t: "⠸⠡⠕⠧⠑⠗⠏⠁⠗⠑⠝"]          # 0x23DC (\overparen)
+ - "⏝": [t: "⠸⠡⠥⠝⠙⠑⠗⠏⠁⠗⠑⠝"]         # 0x23DD (\underparen)
+ - "⏠": [t: "⠸⠡⠕⠧⠑⠗⠎⠓⠑⠇⠇"]          # 0x23E0 (\overshell)
+ - "⏡": [t: "⠸⠡⠥⠝⠙⠑⠗⠎⠓⠑⠇⠇"]         # 0x23E1 (\undershell)
  - "~": [t: "⠈⠱"]               # 0x007E (Tilde)
  - "¬": [t: ""]                 # 0x00AC (Not sign)
  - "¯": [t: "⠱"]                # 0x00AF (bar)
